FreeScout itself is AGPL-3.0
---------------------------
The two modules run inside FreeScout's process. MIT is compatible with the
GPL family, so these files stay MIT, while anyone who distributes them
together with FreeScout distributes that combination under the AGPL. That is
the usual arrangement for community modules and needs nothing further from us.

No FreeScout code was copied here
---------------------------------
The modules call FreeScout rather than reproduce it: replies go through
Conversation::createUserThread and the UserReplied event, the web login uses
Auth::login, and the model constants are referenced, not restated. If that
ever changes and FreeScout code is copied into a file, that file becomes
AGPL-3.0 and has to say so at the top.

Where the OAuth code comes from
-------------------------------
The authorization server in server/ — Client ID Metadata Documents instead of
dynamic registration, PKCE S256, loopback redirects matched without the port,
the RFC 8707 resource check — derives from levino/surveys (MIT,
(c) 2026 Levin Keller), which is the implementation already proven against
Claude. Its MIT notice above covers those parts as well.

Nothing was taken from FreeScout's paid "API & Webhooks" module. Its code was
never available to this project; the feature list it inspired (API access to
conversations, events worth reacting to) came from the public product page at
https://freescout.net/module/api-webhooks/ — facts about what a program does,
not its expression.
